        "source_sha256": "c9e96ffa1a0d3dbab6773d5b0b8ad94517de07e051dff2a9efc1d7624444272a",
        "text": "Government that works for all of San Francisco.\nFor nearly two decades, Joaquín Torres has worked to make San Francisco's government fairer, more accessible, and more connected to the people it serves. As Assessor-Recorder, he brings that commitment to an office that touches the life of every San Franciscan.\n# For everyone who calls this city home.\nSan Francisco is a city of immigrants, entrepreneurs, working families, artists, and neighborhood institutions. Joaquín believes government must be a genuine partner in supporting all of them, and his record is proof of that commitment.\nAbout Joaquín\n# Building\nsomething that lasts.\nEvery San Franciscan deserves access to what this office provides. Every property owner should pay their fair share. And when Joaquín leaves this office, it will be in better shape than when he arrived. That work is ongoing.\nGet involved\ninfo@joaquintorressf.com\nPaid for by Joaquin Torres for Assessor-Recorder 2026.\nFinancial disclosures are available at sfethics.org.",
        "text_limited": false,
        "title": "Joaquin Torres for Assessor",
        "unresolved_images": []
      }
